From: port95 backport <port95@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] port95: erofs: use the C LZ4 decoder instead of lz4armv8 (in-place)

Reverts the EROFS side of 15f150fba66d / 97ea670c1f09 only: z_erofs_lz4_decompress
calls LZ4_decompress_safe{,_partial} again (upstream behaviour). Other users of
LZ4_arm64_decompress_safe (zram/crypto lz4, f2fs, incfs, unlz4) pass dip=false and
are untouched.

Evidence: boot attempt 2 dm-0 "z_erofs_lz4_decompress: failed to decompress -3901
in[4096, 0] out[4492]". -3901 is the C tail's error at input offset 3900 after the
asm hand-over; all 55 system_a.img files that contain a 4096->4492 pcluster pass
fsck.erofs (liblz4), so the on-disk data is valid. EROFS is the only caller passing
dip=true, where lz4armv8 Done1 rewrites the source token in place.

NOT BUILT, NOT RUNTIME-TESTED (VPS unreachable, local compile disallowed).
---
--- a/fs/erofs/decompressor.c
+++ b/fs/erofs/decompressor.c
@@ -222,22 +222,18 @@
 		return PTR_ERR(src);
 
 	/* legacy format could compress extra data in a pcluster. */
+	/*
+	 * port95: use the reference C decoder. The lz4armv8 fast path with dip=inplace_io
+	 * rewrites the source and over-copies past the 48-byte in-place margin
+	 * (boot attempt 2: "failed to decompress -3901 in[4096, 0] out[4492]" on data
+	 * that fsck.erofs/liblz4 decodes cleanly).
+	 */
 	if (rq->partial_decoding || !support_0padding)
-#if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && defined(CONFIG_KERNEL_MODE_NEON)
-		ret = LZ4_arm64_decompress_safe_partial(src + inputmargin, out,
-				rq->inputsize, rq->outputsize, rq->inplace_io);
-#else
 		ret = LZ4_decompress_safe_partial(src + inputmargin, out,
 				rq->inputsize, rq->outputsize, rq->outputsize);
-#endif
 	else
-#if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && defined(CONFIG_KERNEL_MODE_NEON)
-		ret = LZ4_arm64_decompress_safe(src + inputmargin, out,
-					  rq->inputsize, rq->outputsize, rq->inplace_io);
-#else
 		ret = LZ4_decompress_safe(src + inputmargin, out,
 					  rq->inputsize, rq->outputsize);
-#endif
 
 	if (ret != rq->outputsize) {
 		erofs_err(rq->sb, "failed to decompress %d in[%u, %u] out[%u]",
